{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "kind": "installed-cpython-native-lean-resource-leases",
  "date": "2026-11-23",
  "nodes": [
    1221,
    1222,
    1223
  ],
  "scope": "Separate Linux x86-64 CPython 3.11.16 and 3.12.14 ABI wheels on Lean 4.32.2, GCC 12.2.0 and glibc 2.36. Both ordinary and compiler-reviewed synchronous Desk and asyncio Depot share the source-owned Shared.Ticket and Shared.Badge; a third wheel deliberately changes the definition. Includes selector wakeup on native runtime retirement.",
  "checks": [
    "Each ABI has five original component wheels and the shared runtime dependency. pip restored three components offline on each author route. All archive RECORD file hashes and all installed payloads were checked. The clients then ran from relocated installs without developer tools or access to the wheel feed; tampered ledger bytes were rejected even after a good peer had loaded its copy.",
    "Canonical CPython classes shared between compatible packages, rejection of a same-named foreign type and wrong kind, no construction or subclassing, independent retain/close, borrowed inputs, mutable identity and original callback exceptions. Direct and async EIO errors and stream step errors carry independently owned resource values.",
    "Real tasks and pull streams: successful delivery, cooperative cancellation and late discarded results, copies of Python references versus independent leases, exhaustion, early close, cancellation after an item, and a worker-thread finalizer whose release is drained in the other package. Both compatible component load orders and a foreign-first process ended with one native runtime, three initialized components and zero live identities or leaked /dev/null descriptors.",
    "Retiring the runtime alone wakes both already-blocked asyncio waiters. No unrelated callback or completion is needed. An open cursor releases its resources without running its application close hook; epoll and eventfd descriptor counts return to baseline.",
    "mypy checks the actual installed stubs on both author routes: cross-package annotations, isinstance narrowing, declared EIO/step error payloads and three wrong-kind or foreign-definition rejections. The public stubs do not expose ledger words or pointers.",
    "The complete ordinary CPython 3.11 Desk handoff (runtime and component wheels, receipt and elaboration evidence) was reproduced from a second independent path. The producer rejects extension bytes containing its staging root or CPython SDK include path."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Local release evidence, not hosted CI or registry publication. Python-owned host imports and resource-containing compound values have separate contracts.",
    "The resource routes require the process main thread in the main interpreter. Creating a coroutine or an async iterator does not start Lean; keep its borrowed inputs open until it starts."
  ],
  "reproduce": [
    "Use a clean directory for each ABI and a matching Linux x86-64 CPython/Lean toolchain. Set LEAN_BRIDGE_LEAN_PREFIX and LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON to those installations. The application needs no compiler or JavaScript after pip install.",
    "LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_BUILD=$EVIDENCE node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/python-resource-installed.mjs",
    "Use mypy 1.18.2 in an independent verification environment. LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_CAPTURE=$EVIDENCE LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_MYPY=/path/to/mypy node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/python-resource-installed.mjs",
    "LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_REPLAY=$EVIDENCE LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_COMPARE_SOURCES=1 LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_MYPY=/path/to/mypy LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_EXPECTED=docs/evidence/python-resource-leases-20261123.json node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/python-resource-installed.mjs",
    "For the separate scalar regression, set LEAN_BRIDGE_HOST_OBJECT_TEST=1, LEAN_BRIDGE_HOST_PYTHON to the matching Python executable, and LEAN_BRIDGE_HOST_OBJECT_EVIDENCE_DIR to a clean location. Run node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"offline installed Lean tasks wake\" tests/helpers/lean-task-installed.mjs.",
    "For independent-root reproduction, set LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_ROUTE=ordinary and LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_ROLE=desk and build into a separate clean root. Point LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_ORIGINAL and LEAN_BRIDGE_PYTHON_LEASE_INDEPENDENT at the two roots and rerun the test."
  ],
